---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---

<Base title="How It Works" description="How to design and order your personalized photo frame: choose a template, upload photos, preview live, order on WhatsApp.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h1>How it works</h1>

      <h2>1 · Choose a frame template</h2>
      <p>
        Browse the <a href="/frames">template gallery</a>. Each template shows its photo positions, the number of
        photos it needs, available sizes and prices up front.
      </p>

      <h2>2 · Upload your photos</h2>
      <p>
        Tap any photo slot to add a picture straight from your phone or computer. Drag to reposition and use the zoom
        slider to crop each photo exactly how you want it. Add your name, message or date in the text fields.
        Your photos stay on your device while you design — nothing is uploaded until you place the order.
      </p>

      <h2>3 · Watch the live preview</h2>
      <p>
        The preview updates instantly as you edit — the same layout, crop and text we print. Switch sizes and frame
        finishes (black, white, dark brown or gallery-wrap canvas) and see the price change live.
      </p>

      <h2>4 · Order on WhatsApp</h2>
      <p>
        Happy with the design? Tap <strong>Order on WhatsApp</strong>. Your order summary and the preview image are
        shared to our WhatsApp chat — attach your original photos there so we can print them at full quality. We
        confirm the design, you pay securely, and production begins.
      </p>

      <h2>5 · Printed, packed and shipped</h2>
      <p>
        Orders are processed within {site.shipping.processing_days}. For special occasions, order at least
        {site.shipping.occasion_lead_days} working days ahead. Shipping is free on orders above
        ₹{site.shipping.free_above}; a flat ₹{site.shipping.flat_fee} applies below that.
      </p>

      <p><a class="btn btn--primary" href="/frames">Start creating</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
